###
### 17. Test Cancel Already Completed Migration (Should Fail)
###
# POST {{baseUrl}}/api/migrations/completed-migration-id/cancel
# Content-Type: {{contentType}}

###
### NOTES:
### 
### 1. Replace @migrationId variable with actual migration ID from responses
### 2. Update real store credentials in sections 11-12 before testing with actual stores
### 3. The API uses these BigCommerce fields:
###    - storeId: Your BigCommerce store hash (e.g., "v6q95r5n91")
###    - accessToken: Your BigCommerce API access token
###    - channelId: Channel ID (usually "1" for main storefront)
### 4. Expected responses:
###    - POST /migrations: 202 Accepted with migration details
###    - GET /migrations: 200 OK with migration list (or 204 if empty)
###    - GET /migrations/{id}: 200 OK with migration status
###    - POST /migrations/{id}/cancel: 200 OK with cancellation confirmation
### 5. Error responses will be 400 Bad Request, 404 Not Found, or 500 Internal Server Error
### 